WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:03.825
Meet Bunker Evolved.

00:00:03.825 --> 00:00:10.515
A free, open-source ambient instrument for your M-VAVE F M One.

00:00:10.515 --> 00:00:12.339
Four musical layers.

00:00:12.339 --> 00:00:14.164
Sixty-four sound presets.

00:00:14.164 --> 00:00:15.988
Twenty-four complete worlds.

00:00:15.988 --> 00:00:19.029
And thirty-two scales to explore.

00:00:19.029 --> 00:00:25.719
Start with a world, press play, and let the music breathe.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:39.262
Choose a world while playback is stopped, then press octave plus
to load it.

00:00:39.262 --> 00:00:44.060
Use Algorithm to choose Air, Melody, Root, or Spark.

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:46.192
These are musical roles.

00:00:46.192 --> 00:00:50.456
Every layer can use its own synthesis engine.

00:00:50.456 --> 00:00:54.187
Home moves between the six Bunker pages.

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.833
For a new melody, open Grow.

00:01:02.833 --> 00:01:07.659
The four knobs choose the root note, scale, style, and target.

00:01:07.659 --> 00:01:10.731
Tune fits your notes to the scale.

00:01:10.731 --> 00:01:12.486
Soft makes small changes.

00:01:12.486 --> 00:01:13.802
Flow moves further.

00:01:13.802 --> 00:01:17.312
New reshapes the phrase over its existing rhythm.

00:01:17.312 --> 00:01:19.506
Press octave plus to apply.

00:01:19.506 --> 00:01:23.455
Press octave minus to undo the last Grow step.

00:01:23.455 --> 00:01:26.088
Your sound and mix stay intact.

00:01:26.088 --> 00:01:30.476
Grow locks the new phrase, giving you time to listen.

00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:38.050
Want more control?

00:01:38.050 --> 00:01:45.799
Sound gives each layer sixteen starting points, with quick
controls for colour, release, and reverb.

00:01:45.799 --> 00:01:51.481
Edit, Envelope, L F O, and Effects open the deeper tools.

00:01:51.481 --> 00:01:56.647
The step sequencer lets you change individual notes and chords.

00:01:56.647 --> 00:02:01.813
Save the complete composition in one of four project slots.

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:12.347
To let a phrase develop by itself, open Evolve.

00:02:12.347 --> 00:02:18.277
Choose a process, its probability, and the number of loops
between changes.

00:02:18.277 --> 00:02:25.689
Try Walk for gentle melodic movement, or Breath for changes in
touch and rhythm probability.

00:02:25.689 --> 00:02:31.619
Octave minus locks the current phrase whenever you want to keep
it.

00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:45.171
To install, charge your F M One and connect it directly with a
USB data cable.

00:02:45.171 --> 00:02:51.241
Open the installer in desktop Chrome, close other MIDI apps, and
click Detect.

00:02:51.241 --> 00:02:54.510
Stock firmware uses the same update protocol.

00:02:54.510 --> 00:02:58.712
There is no need to install Amb One first.

00:02:58.712 --> 00:03:05.716
Back up your music, choose Bunker Evolved, read the recovery
guide, and start the update.

00:03:05.716 --> 00:03:11.320
Keep power and USB connected until the final firmware identity
is confirmed.

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:27.172
The recovery page includes the previous Bunker build, Amb One,
and a verified original V fifteen file from M-VAVE.

00:03:27.172 --> 00:03:33.858
An interrupted transfer can be restarted if the MIDI update
loader still responds.

00:03:33.858 --> 00:03:41.058
The watchdog can restart a stalled application, but it cannot
repair every failed flash.

00:03:41.058 --> 00:03:45.173
A chip recovery mode may need separate tools.

00:03:45.173 --> 00:03:48.773
Firmware rollback does not restore overwritten music.

00:03:54.800 --> 00:04:01.763
Bunker Evolved is built on Felucca, with gratitude to the open-
source FM One community.

00:04:01.763 --> 00:04:06.737
The project owner has tested this build on real hardware.

00:04:06.737 --> 00:04:14.198
Explore the browser instrument, hear the worlds, read the guide,
and download the complete source.

00:04:14.198 --> 00:04:15.690
Free to play.

00:04:15.690 --> 00:04:17.183
Free to explore.

00:04:17.183 --> 00:04:19.172
Make something that grows.
